Follow the system's fontconfig settings when rasterizing text on Linux and FreeBSD.

GPUI's cosmic-text/swash path always hinted, always recommended subpixel rendering and
took the subpixel order only from wl_output / Xft.rgba. This asks fontconfig (opened at
runtime through yeslogic-fontconfig-sys's dlopen feature, so nothing new is linked) what it
would give a renderer for each family, per Qt and cairo, and applies it:
  antialias false        -> grayscale mask thresholded to 1 bit (swash can't do mono)
  rgba none/unknown      -> TextRenderingMode::Grayscale
  rgba rgb/bgr           -> subpixel in that order, over the display's report
  rgba vrgb/vbgr         -> grayscale (swash has no vertical subpixel format)
  rgba unset             -> unchanged: subpixel, display's order
  hinting false / hintstyle none -> swash hinting off; slight/medium/full -> on (swash is binary)
No libfontconfig, or other platforms: the old behaviour. An application's explicit
text_rendering_mode still wins over the recommendation.

